{
  "sticker": "urchin",
  "called": "the sea urchin",
  "skeleton": "round sea urchin facing the viewer: root on the ground under the ball; body with a belly bone carrying the spiny ball (squash; turns a little so the spines wiggle); face on the body with eyes, mouth and brows. A fanned-spines ball and a spines-tucked ball swap in for the body.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a cheerful round purple sea urchin character. Draw this exact sea urchin as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the sea urchin: the round purple sea urchin with all its soft pink-tipped spines, as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the rosy cheeks.\n2. the same sea urchin with its spines fanned out wide: every spine longer and straighter, spread out all round like a starburst, with the same blank face and rosy cheeks.\n3. the same sea urchin with its spines folded down flat and close against its round body, smaller and smooth, with the same blank face and rosy cheeks.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or another part) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a cheerful round purple sea urchin character; image 2 shows the same sea urchin cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the sea urchin's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the sea urchin in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a dark round eye with a big white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the same eye squeezed shut, crying: a tight, creased, downward-curving closed line.\n7. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile line.\n8. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n9. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n10. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n11. the mouth open in a wobbly crying wail, its corners turned down, the inside pink.\n12. one eyebrow: a small, thin, softly curved dark brown line.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
